# Line endings
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` (Windows default) checks files out with CRLF. That
# is harmless for most text, but it breaks two things in this repo:
#
#   1. `.githooks/*` — git runs them through a shell. A CRLF shebang or a
#      stray CR inside `case`/`[[ ]]` makes the hook fail, and a hook that
#      fails silently is worse than no hook at all (pushes get rejected
#      with a confusing "bad interpreter" message).
#   2. `tools/*.sh` — same reason.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the worktree copy to LF regardless of the local
# `core.autocrlf` setting, so every clone gets a runnable script.
# `text` keeps git normalising on commit.

.githooks/**  text eol=lf
tools/*.sh    text eol=lf
tools/*.mjs   text eol=lf

# Go sources are formatted by gofmt, which requires LF.
*.go          text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
